/evanrawal.bsky.social/post/3n36ykr6g4k2q"},{"a":"Evan Rawal","d":"2026-11-23T18:52:30+00:00","h":"evanrawal.bsky.social","o":"Denver Gazette","t":"There are the obvious. With no MacKinnon, Brock Nelson and Nazem Kadri have to step up.\n\nBut who has the most at stake or can quiet some folks without MacKinnon for the next 12 weeks?\n\nwww.denvergazette.com/2026/11/23/w...","u":"https://bsky.app/profile/evanrawal.bsky.social/post/3n2ysgdgul22j"},{"a":"Evan Rawal","d":"2026-11-21T21:00:50+00:00","h":"evanrawal.bsky.social","o":"Denver Gazette","t":"Can the Avalanche survive without Nathan MacKinnon? They have to now. \n\nThe superstar is now out 12 weeks, which puts his return for around the All Star break.\n\nIt’s Nelson and Kadri time. \n\n“The matchups are going to get tougher for some of them.”\n\nwww.denvergazette.com/2026/11/21/a...","u":"https://bsky.app/profile/evanrawal.bsky.social/post/3n2tynx63o22o"},{"a":"Corey Masisak","d":"2026-11-20T23:11:44+00:00","h":"cmasisak22.bsky.social","o":"Denver Post","t":"Avs have been one of the NHL's best on the second half of a B2B for years, but only so-so so far this season. \n\nLast night was a vintage performance, led by Brock Nelson, strong defensive work and Scott Wedgewood's best night of the year.\n\nwww.denverpost.com/2026/11/19/a...","u":"https://bsky.app/profile/cmasisak22.bsky.social/post/3n2rpj4abgc2t"}],"team":"COL","threads":[],"videos":[{"d":"2026-11-14T19:03:07+00:00","id":"eKEypjdzakw","k":"video","t":"Brock Nelson hit a celly 😂","team":"COL","u":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eKEypjdzakw"},{"d":"2026-11-11T01:35:34+00:00","id":"MVhaFDegEnM","k":"video","t":"Nelson gets the first 🚨","team":"COL","u":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MVhaFDegEnM"}]}